      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy')  # (8000, 1024) float32, read-only usage\n    X = np.ascontiguousarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n    N, D = X.shape\n\n    # ---- Compute row squared norms in float64 precision, chunked to save memory ----\n    norms = np.empty(N, dtype=np.float64)\n    norm_chunk = 1000\n    for i in range(0, N, norm_chunk):\n        blk = X[i:i + norm_chunk].astype(np.float64)\n        norms[i:i + norm_chunk] = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', blk, blk)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    block = 200  # rows per block to bound memory usage\n\n    Xt = X.T  # view, no copy (transpose just changes strides)\n\n    for i in range(0, N, block):\n        Xi = X[i:i + block]                 # (b, D) float32\n        G = Xi @ Xt                         # (b, N) float32, BLAS matmul\n        G64 = G.astype(np.float64)          # promote for precision\n        ni = norms[i:i + block][:, None]\n        nj = norms[None, :]\n        d2 = ni + nj - 2.0 * G64\n        np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n        np.sqrt(d2, out=d2)\n        total += d2.sum()\n\n        # free temporaries explicitly\n        del G, G64, d2\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.6f}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
